In news:<1129096519.638332.188910@o13g2000cwo.googlegroups.com>, Gherkin 
<gherkinz@hotmail.com> says...
> I have played nethack for years and just downloaded SLASH'EM for the
> first time.  However, the interface seems quite different, and I would
> prefer to play with ASCII characters.  Is it possible to play SLASHEM
> in ASCII graphics and with the same commands as regular nethack?  Maybe
> this is a stupid question, but I know very little about Nethack beyond
> how to enter my name and play.

Either set "OPTIONS=windowtype:tty" in defaults.nh (see the Guidebook - 
http://nethack.org/v343/Guidebook.html - that comes with Nethack and 
SlashEM about defaults.nh), or select one of the 'ASCII' choices in the 
Map drop-down menu after starting a non-TTY SlashEM session.
"windowtype:tty" makes SlashEM play in a 'traditional DOS Window' while 
changing the 'Map' setting gives you ASCII characters in a 'normal 
Windows window'. I'm not sure which one it is that you want.

There is not so much difference in the commands, and some are IMO better 
implemented in SlashEM than in vanilla Nethack. Perhaps you could try 
them out and see if you like them. (A common problem for new players are 
that they can't find out how to eat(/etc) something that lies on the 
ground, use the comma key, after 'e'(/etc), to do this.)

These are the settings that I use (except the standard ones) in 
default.nh:

OPTIONS=lit_corridor,showdmg,showweight,time,map_mode:ascii8x12,color,IB
Mgraphics,eight_bit_tty,use_inverse,nolegacy,autodig,!
mail,menustyle:full,msghistory:200,!
news,number_pad:2,race:random,gender:random,role:random,align:random,run
mode:walk,scores:10 top/10 
around/own,showexp,standout,suppress_alert:0.0.7,!tombstone,hilite_pet,!
splash_screen,!
autopickup,msg_window:c,name:MyName,dogname:MyDogName,catname:MyCatName,
horsename:MyHorseName,fruit:MyFruit

BOULDER=233

